Set A = {1, 2, 3, 4}
Set B = {3, 4, 5, 6}

The union of A and B, denoted as A ∪ B, includes all unique elements from both sets. So, we combine the elements and remove any duplicates:

A ∪ B = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}

Now, we count the number of elements in the union set A ∪ B:

|A ∪ B| = 6

